\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Voltage against applied current}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{\citet{§3.4, p. 56}{ermentrout2010mathematical} varies the
applied current in the Hopf column of Table 3.1. For each current
there is one equilibrium. Figure 3.4a on p. 57 draws the voltage of
that equilibrium against the current, together with the extreme
voltages on periodic orbits. On that figure, solid curves are the
stable solutions and dashed curves are the unstable ones.
\citet{§6.1, p. 159}{izhikevich2007dynamical} takes the injected
current as the parameter and asks how the rest state changes.}
